      "round": 1,
      "round_summary": "Round 1: Fix `usb_rst_consistent` and `usb_rst_stable` (DUT bug). Root cause: the counting condition used registered `!usb_rst_reg` instead of combinational `rst_cnt =/= 31.U`, causing a one-cycle drift where `rst_cnt` wraps/gets reset while `usb_rst_reg` latches true. Fix: (1) Added combinational wire `usb_rst_terminal = rst_cnt === 31.U` and used `!usb_rst_terminal` in the counting `elsewhen` to stop counting immediately when terminal count is reached. (2) Added `usb_rst_reg := false.B` inside the `when(!io.rst)` block (lines 76-77) so external reset clears `usb_rst_reg` synchronously, preventing the stale-latch scenario. (3) Updated the liveness antecedent to use `!usb_rst_terminal` instead of `!usb_rst_reg` for consistency. Assertion labels `usb_rst_consistent` and `usb_rst_stable` preserved. No homologous assertions found.",
