      "round": 2,
      "round_summary": "Round 2: Fix `usb_rst_consistent` and `usb_rst_stable` (DUT bug). Root cause: unconditional assignment `usb_rst_reg := usb_rst_terminal` (line 159) sits outside the `when`-`elsewhen` chain. In Chisel-generated Verilog, non-blocking assignments execute in textual order and the last write wins, so this outer assignment overrides `usb_rst_reg := false.B` inside `when(!io.rst)`. When `io.rst` falls (0) concurrently with `rst_cnt` reaching 31, the counter resets to 0 but `usb_rst_reg` incorrectly latches true from the overridden terminal signal, causing the `!usb_rst_reg || rst_cnt === 31.U` check to fail one cycle later. Fix: removed the standalone `usb_rst_reg := usb_rst_terminal` and added `.elsewhen(usb_rst_terminal) { usb_rst_reg := true.B }` as the last branch of the `when` chain, giving `when(!io.rst)` priority to clear `usb_rst_reg` before the terminal-set branch can fire. This ensures `usb_rst_reg` transitions synchronously within the same ordered `when` block, eliminating the override. Assertion labels `usb_rst_consistent` and `usb_rst_stable` preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions found.",
